{"id": "EUVD-2026-104315", "enisaUuid": "0a42ebcb-344d-378a-beea-bdc979a9f77f", "description": "Sigma File Manager through 2.2.0 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability because validate_remote_url() in security.rs never checks resolved IP addresses for extension download commands. A malicious extension or catalog entry can use hostnames resolving to loopback, private, or cloud metadata addresses to read internal responses via files written to the extension directory.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T02:46:37", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/aleksey-hoffman/sigma-file-manager/issues/552", "https://github.com/aleksey-hoffman/sigma-file-manager/commit/45cedf892f800c6b140b0e3cd6e55fdbcf2cf479", "https://github.com/aleksey-hoffman/sigma-file-manager/blob/v2.2.0/src-tauri/src/extensions/security.rs", "https://github.com/aleksey-hoffman/sigma-file-manager/blob/v2.2.0/src-tauri/src/extensions/filesystem.rs", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sigma-file-manager-through-2.2.0-ssrf-via-extension-download-commands"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111936", "GHSA-37hh-79v8-v8vr"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e3d4933b-5e81-3f77-8907-3a30202902e0", "product": {"name": "Sigma File Manager", "vendor": {"name": "aleksey-hoffman"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "93ee87f9-ea52-3226-87c8-4de890c86de0", "vendor": {"name": "aleksey-hoffman"}}], "isExploited": false}